--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party code
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The default native build has no runtime dependencies. The optional `wasm`
feature uses the `wasm-bindgen` family of crates for JavaScript bindings; their
licence notices are supplied by Cargo metadata and the generated package.
Everything under src/ is original work, including the SHA-256 implementation in
src/parser_core/hash.rs (written against the FIPS 180-4 specification and
validated against its published test vectors).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Reference data
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Linguistic reference artifacts under resources/ are original compilations
prepared for this project. They are NOT derived from LanguageTool, nlprule,
Harper, or any treebank distribution.

Per-artifact source, licence, normalization policy, generation method, and
checksum are recorded in resources/en/rulepack.manifest and docs/RESOURCES.md.

Tokenization split points follow the Penn Treebank *convention* — that is, the
conventional places to divide contractions and clitics. Conventions are not
copyrightable; no Penn Treebank data is included or required.

Gold annotations under fixtures/ are hand-written for this project. Any corpus
added later must arrive with explicit per-component licence terms, recorded in
docs/RESOURCES.md before merge. See CONTRIBUTING.md, "The linguistic resource
rule".
